{
  "title": "Dimglass Coast - Lanterns Along the Tide (r2 remaster pilot)",
  "_note": "R2 REMASTER PILOT (parallel to dimglass-coast-a; NOT wired into the game). Panel brief: docs/reviews/music-remaster-panel.md. The first open road. 126 BPM, 4/4, G major with a borrowed bVI-bVII (Ebmaj7-F) 'open sea' lift in the bridge. Form A(8) A'(8) B(8) A''(8) = 32 bars, ~61 s. The hook is the LANTERN CALL bounced: D5-G5-A5 (sol-do-re) on a syncopated 'q e q.' stride, settling B5-A5-G5; an A4-B4 pickup throws the loop back to the top. A: lead + skipping 'boom-ba' bass + bell-buoy harp chimes on the OFFBEATS (forward drive) + light kit. A': strings enter (guide tones); the cadence detours through B7 (V/vi) and A7 (V/V). B: modal-mixture bridge (Cmaj7-Bm7-Am7-D7-Ebmaj7-F-Am7-D7) - the lead calls in 2-bar spans and the flute answers in the gaps, the bass walks, the harp rolls in waves, the kit opens up (open hat, 'sea-spray'). A'': the tune returns doubled at the octave by the flute, bells on the phrase ends. ECHO = composed SNES echo (lead a dotted eighth late, wrapped across the seam). <=8 voices. Original melody throughout (VISION.md).",
